MoonLib - Simple Usage Guide
============================

This guide is based on the current ClassicInterface version of MoonLib.

The library is loaded using an executor with loadstring:

local MoonLib = loadstring(game:HttpGet("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MoonOFCC/RobloxGUI_Moonlight_Libraries/refs/heads/main/Moonlight%20Classic%20Library/Moonlight-Library_ClassicInterface_V2.lua"))()

The value returned by loadstring is the MoonLib library object.

--------------------------------------------------
-- CREATE A WINDOW
--------------------------------------------------

local Window = MoonLib:CreateWindow(
    "Player Controls"
)

CreateWindow parameters:

MoonLib:CreateWindow(
    WindowTitle,
    WindowImage
)

WindowTitle:
    The text displayed at the top of the GUI.

WindowImage:
    Optional image displayed next to the window title.

    It can be:

    "rbxassetid://123456789"
    123456789
    "https://your-image-url"

Example:

local Window = MoonLib:CreateWindow(
    "My GUI",
    "rbxassetid://123456789"
)

The returned Window object is used to create tabs and control the GUI.

--------------------------------------------------
-- CREATE A TAB
--------------------------------------------------

local PlayerTab = Window:CreateTab(
    "Player",
    nil,
    1
)

CreateTab parameters:

Window:CreateTab(
    TabName,
    TabImage,
    IndexPosition
)

TabName:
    The name shown inside the sidebar.

TabImage:
    Optional image shown beside the tab name.

    It can be:

    "rbxassetid://123456789"
    123456789
    "https://your-image-url"

    If no image is provided, the library shows the first letter
    of the tab name instead.

IndexPosition:
    Controls the order of the tabs in the sidebar.

Example:

local PlayerTab = Window:CreateTab(
    "Player",
    "rbxassetid://123456789",
    1
)

local SettingsTab = Window:CreateTab(
    "Settings",
    "rbxassetid://987654321",
    2
)

The first created tab is automatically selected.

--------------------------------------------------
-- CREATE A LABEL
--------------------------------------------------

PlayerTab:CreateLabel(
    "This is a normal label.",
    1
)

CreateLabel parameters:

Tab:CreateLabel(
    Text,
    IndexPosition,
    TextColor
)

Text:
    The text displayed by the label.

IndexPosition:
    Controls the position of the label inside the tab.

TextColor:
    Optional Color3 value for the text.

Example:

PlayerTab:CreateLabel(
    "Player Settings",
    1,
    Color3.fromRGB(255, 255, 255)
)

The label returns the TextLabel instance.

--------------------------------------------------
-- CREATE A SECTION HEADER
--------------------------------------------------

PlayerTab:CreateHeader(
    "Player Settings",
    "Change your player options below.",
    1
)

CreateHeader parameters:

Tab:CreateHeader(
    HeaderTitle,
    HeaderSubtitle,
    IndexPosition
)

HeaderTitle:
    Large text displayed as the section title.

HeaderSubtitle:
    Smaller text displayed underneath the title.

IndexPosition:
    Controls the position inside the tab.

Example:

PlayerTab:CreateHeader(
    "Movement",
    "Customize your movement settings.",
    1
)

This is useful for separating different parts of a tab.

--------------------------------------------------
-- CREATE AN INFORMATION CARD
--------------------------------------------------

PlayerTab:CreateInfoCard(
    "Movement",
    "Customize your character movement values.",
    Window.Theme.Blue,
    2
)

CreateInfoCard parameters:

Tab:CreateInfoCard(
    CardTitle,
    CardDescription,
    AccentColor,
    IndexPosition
)

CardTitle:
    The title displayed on the card.

CardDescription:
    The description displayed below the title.

AccentColor:
    The color used for the card outline and side accent.

IndexPosition:
    Controls the position inside the tab.

Example:

PlayerTab:CreateInfoCard(
    "Warning",
    "Some games may reset movement values.",
    Window.Theme.Red,
    3
)

Available default theme colors include:

Window.Theme.Blue
Window.Theme.BlueLight
Window.Theme.BlueDark
Window.Theme.Green
Window.Theme.Red
Window.Theme.Yellow
Window.Theme.Purple
Window.Theme.Text
Window.Theme.SecondaryText
Window.Theme.MutedText
Window.Theme.Panel
Window.Theme.Card
Window.Theme.BrightBorder
Window.Theme.Border

Use Window.Theme instead of MoonLib.Theme.

--------------------------------------------------
-- CREATE A STAT CARD
--------------------------------------------------

PlayerTab:CreateStatCard(
    "Current Speed",
    "32",
    Window.Theme.Blue,
    4
)

CreateStatCard parameters:

Tab:CreateStatCard(
    StatTitle,
    StatValue,
    AccentColor,
    IndexPosition
)

StatTitle:
    The smaller title shown above the value.

StatValue:
    The large value shown on the card.

AccentColor:
    The color used for the value and outline.

IndexPosition:
    Controls the position inside the tab.

Example:

PlayerTab:CreateStatCard(
    "JumpPower",
    "75",
    Window.Theme.Green,
    5
)

--------------------------------------------------
-- CREATE A BUTTON
--------------------------------------------------

PlayerTab:CreateButton(
    "Reset Settings",
    function()
        print("The reset button was clicked.")
    end,
    Window.Theme.Red,
    6
)

CreateButton parameters:

Tab:CreateButton(
    ButtonText,
    CallbackFunction,
    CustomColor,
    IndexPosition
)

ButtonText:
    The text displayed on the button.

CallbackFunction:
    The function that runs when the button is clicked.

CustomColor:
    Optional Color3 value for the button background and outline.

IndexPosition:
    Controls the position inside the tab.

Example:

PlayerTab:CreateButton(
    "Print Message",
    function()
        print("Hello from MoonLib.")
    end,
    nil,
    7
)

A button returns the TextButton instance.

--------------------------------------------------
-- CREATE A TOGGLE
--------------------------------------------------

local SpeedToggle = PlayerTab:CreateToggle(
    "Speed + Jump Boost",
    false,
    function(enabled)
        print("Toggle state:", enabled)
    end,
    8
)

CreateToggle parameters:

Tab:CreateToggle(
    ToggleText,
    DefaultState,
    CallbackFunction,
    IndexPosition,
    CustomColor
)

ToggleText:
    The text shown beside the switch.

DefaultState:
    true means the toggle starts enabled.

    false means the toggle starts disabled.

CallbackFunction:
    Runs whenever the toggle changes.

    The callback receives one value:

    enabled

    enabled is either true or false.

IndexPosition:
    Controls the position inside the tab.

CustomColor:
    Optional Color3 value for the toggle container.

Example:

local FlyToggle = PlayerTab:CreateToggle(
    "Enable Feature",
    false,
    function(enabled)
        if enabled then
            print("Feature enabled.")
        else
            print("Feature disabled.")
        end
    end,
    9
)

Toggle methods:

SpeedToggle:GetValue()

    Returns true or false depending on the current state.

Example:

if SpeedToggle:GetValue() then
    print("The toggle is currently enabled.")
end

SpeedToggle:SetValue(
    true,
    true
)

The first argument is the new state.

The second argument controls whether the callback should run.

Example:

SpeedToggle:SetValue(true, false)

This enables the toggle without running its callback.

SpeedToggle:Toggle()

Switches the toggle to the opposite state.

Example:

SpeedToggle:Toggle()

SpeedToggle:Destroy()

Removes the toggle from the GUI.

--------------------------------------------------
-- CREATE A SLIDER
--------------------------------------------------

local SpeedSlider = PlayerTab:CreateSlider(
    "WalkSpeed",
    false,
    function(enabled, value)
        print("Slider enabled:", enabled)
        print("Slider value:", value)
    end,
    32,
    16,
    100,
    10
)

CreateSlider parameters:

Tab:CreateSlider(
    SliderText,
    DefaultState,
    CallbackFunction,
    DefaultValue,
    MinimumValue,
    MaximumValue,
    IndexPosition,
    CustomColor
)

SliderText:
    The text shown above the slider.

DefaultState:
    The initial enabled state associated with the slider.

DefaultValue:
    The starting value of the slider.

MinimumValue:
    The lowest value the slider can use.

MaximumValue:
    The highest value the slider can use.

IndexPosition:
    Controls the position inside the tab.

CustomColor:
    Optional Color3 value for the slider container.

The slider callback receives two values:

enabled
value

Example:

local PowerSlider = PlayerTab:CreateSlider(
    "Power",
    true,
    function(enabled, value)
        if enabled then
            print("Power is active:", value)
        end
    end,
    50,
    0,
    100,
    11,
    Window.Theme.Blue
)

Slider methods:

PowerSlider:GetValue()

    Returns the current slider value.

PowerSlider:IsEnabled()

    Returns true or false depending on the slider state.

PowerSlider:SetValue(
    75,
    true
)

Sets the slider value to 75.

The second argument controls whether the callback runs.

PowerSlider:SetEnabled(
    true,
    true
)

Changes the enabled state of the slider.

The second argument controls whether the callback runs.

PowerSlider:Destroy()

Removes the slider from the GUI.

--------------------------------------------------
-- CREATE A DROPDOWN
--------------------------------------------------

local ModeDropdown = PlayerTab:CreateDropdown(
    "Movement Mode",
    {
        [1] = "Normal",
        [2] = "Fast",
        [3] = "Extreme",
    },
    function(name, id)
        print("Selected name:", name)
        print("Selected ID:", id)
    end,
    12
)

CreateDropdown parameters:

Tab:CreateDropdown(
    DropdownText,
    OptionsTable,
    CallbackFunction,
    IndexPosition,
    CustomColor,
    MultiSelect
)

DropdownText:
    The title displayed on the dropdown.

OptionsTable:
    A table containing the selectable options.

CallbackFunction:
    Runs when the user selects an option.

    In single-select mode, the callback receives:

    SelectedName
    SelectedID

IndexPosition:
    Controls the position inside the tab.

CustomColor:
    Optional Color3 value for the dropdown header.

MultiSelect:
    Optional multi-selection mode.

    Use:

    true

    or:

    "Multi"

Example of a single-select dropdown:

local ModeDropdown = PlayerTab:CreateDropdown(
    "Movement Mode",
    {
        [1] = "Normal",
        [2] = "Fast",
        [3] = "Extreme",
    },
    function(name, id)
        if name == "Normal" then
            print("Normal mode selected.")
        elseif name == "Fast" then
            print("Fast mode selected.")
        elseif name == "Extreme" then
            print("Extreme mode selected.")
        end
    end,
    13
)

The table keys become the IDs.

The table values become the displayed names.

Example:

{
    [1] = "Normal",
    [2] = "Fast",
    [3] = "Extreme",
}

The names are:

Normal
Fast
Extreme

The IDs are:

1
2
3

Dropdown methods:

ModeDropdown:GetValue()

    Returns the selected name.

ModeDropdown:GetIds()

    Returns the selected ID.

ModeDropdown:GetSelection()

    Returns both selected names and selected IDs.

Example:

local names, ids = ModeDropdown:GetSelection()

print(names[1])
print(ids[1])

ModeDropdown:GetMode()

    Returns:

    "Single"

    or:

    "Multi"

ModeDropdown:SetOpen(
    true
)

Opens the dropdown.

ModeDropdown:SetOpen(
    false
)

Closes the dropdown.

ModeDropdown:SetValue(
    "Fast",
    true
)

Selects the option named "Fast".

The second argument controls whether the callback runs.

You can also select by ID:

ModeDropdown:SetValue(
    2,
    true
)

ModeDropdown:Clear(
    true
)

Clears the selected option.

The argument controls whether the callback runs.

ModeDropdown:Destroy()

Removes the dropdown from the GUI.

--------------------------------------------------
-- MULTI-SELECT DROPDOWN
--------------------------------------------------

local FeaturesDropdown = PlayerTab:CreateDropdown(
    "Features",
    {
        [1] = "Speed",
        [2] = "Jump",
        [3] = "Gravity",
    },
    function(names, ids)
        print("Selected names:")

        for _, name in ipairs(names) do
            print(name)
        end

        print("Selected IDs:")

        for _, id in ipairs(ids) do
            print(id)
        end
    end,
    14,
    nil,
    true
)

The last argument true enables multi-select mode.

You may also use:

"Multi"

instead of true.

In multi-select mode, the callback receives:

SelectedNames
SelectedIDs

Example:

local names, ids = FeaturesDropdown:GetSelection()

FeaturesDropdown:SetValue(
    {
        "Speed",
        "Jump",
    },
    true
)

You can also select using IDs:

FeaturesDropdown:SetValue(
    {
        1,
        2,
    },
    true
)

--------------------------------------------------
-- WINDOW METHODS
--------------------------------------------------

Window:SetTitle(
    "New Window Title"
)

Changes the title displayed at the top of the GUI.

Example:

Window:SetTitle("Updated Player Controls")

Window:SetImage(
    "rbxassetid://123456789"
)

Changes the image next to the window title.

Window:SelectTab(
    "Player"
)

Selects a tab by its name.

Example:

local successful = Window:SelectTab("Settings")

if successful then
    print("Settings tab selected.")
end

Window:Toggle()

Hides the GUI if it is visible.

Shows the GUI if it is hidden.

Window:IsVisible()

Returns true or false depending on whether the window is visible.

Example:

if Window:IsVisible() then
    print("The GUI is visible.")
end

Window:Destroy()

Completely removes the GUI and disconnects its library connections.

Example:

Window:Destroy()

--------------------------------------------------
-- RIGHTSHIFT TOGGLE
--------------------------------------------------

The library automatically listens for the RightShift key.

Pressing RightShift:

    If the GUI is visible, it becomes hidden.

    If the GUI is hidden, it becomes visible.

This feature does not require additional code.

--------------------------------------------------
-- CUSTOM COLORS
--------------------------------------------------

Custom colors must be Color3 values.

Correct:

Window.Theme.Blue

Color3.fromRGB(255, 0, 0)

Color3.new(1, 0, 0)

Example:

PlayerTab:CreateButton(
    "Red Button",
    function()
        print("Clicked.")
    end,
    Color3.fromRGB(200, 40, 50),
    1
)

Do not pass a color as a normal text string.

Incorrect:

"Red"

Correct:

Color3.fromRGB(255, 0, 0)

--------------------------------------------------
-- INDEX POSITIONS
--------------------------------------------------

The IndexPosition controls the order of objects inside a tab.

Example:

PlayerTab:CreateLabel("First", 1)

PlayerTab:CreateButton(
    "Second",
    function()
        print("Second")
    end,
    nil,
    2
)

PlayerTab:CreateToggle(
    "Third",
    false,
    function(enabled)
        print(enabled)
    end,
    3
)

Lower numbers appear first.

If two objects use the same index, their order may depend on when they were created.

--------------------------------------------------
-- COMPLETE EXAMPLE
--------------------------------------------------

local Players = game:GetService("Players")

local Player = Players.LocalPlayer

local MoonLib = loadstring(game:HttpGet(
    "YOUR_RAW_LIBRARY_URL"
))()

local Window = MoonLib:CreateWindow(
    "Player Controls",
    "rbxassetid://123456789"
)

local PlayerTab = Window:CreateTab(
    "Player",
    "rbxassetid://987654321",
    1
)

PlayerTab:CreateHeader(
    "Player Settings",
    "Adjust your movement options.",
    1
)

PlayerTab:CreateInfoCard(
    "Movement",
    "Customize your character's movement values.",
    Window.Theme.Blue,
    2
)

local SpeedToggle = PlayerTab:CreateToggle(
    "Speed + Jump Boost",
    false,
    function(enabled)
        print("Speed and jump boost:", enabled)
    end,
    3
)

local SpeedSlider = PlayerTab:CreateSlider(
    "WalkSpeed",
    false,
    function(enabled, value)
        print("Slider enabled:", enabled)
        print("WalkSpeed value:", value)
    end,
    32,
    16,
    100,
    4
)

PlayerTab:CreateButton(
    "Reset Settings",
    function()
        SpeedToggle:SetValue(false, true)
        SpeedSlider:SetValue(16, true)
    end,
    Window.Theme.Red,
    5
)

local ModeDropdown = PlayerTab:CreateDropdown(
    "Movement Mode",
    {
        [1] = "Normal",
        [2] = "Fast",
        [3] = "Extreme",
    },
    function(name, id)
        print("Selected movement mode:", name, id)
    end,
    6
)

print("MoonLib loaded successfully.")
